    "body": "## Problem\r\nRedundant code\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\ncombine `path_has_wildcard()` and `path_has_exp_wildcard()`\r\ndrop `MB_PTR_ADV` in path.c\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n  Thank you for contributing to Neovim!\r\n  If this is your first time, check out https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-requests-prs\r\n  for our PR guidelines.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nNote: I'm not entirely convinced they're worth combining. If adding another parameter ends up making the code less readable, I'm really fine with closing this instead.\r\nI mainly brought it up because they have similar logic. Also, path_has_exp_wildcard() operates on whatever wildcard syntax remains after shell/env/backtick expansion, so the two felt somewhat related.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-22T14:39:29Z",
